# Cursor Rules — Unified AWS Bedrock Controller (Go / AWS SDK for Go v2)

## Project purpose
- Build a **single, unified Kubernetes controller** (one Go controller) to manage AWS Bedrock resources.
- Language: Go (>= 1.22). SDK: **AWS SDK for Go v2** (pinned).
- Iterative development: implement one thin slice at a time with **unit tests that must pass before advancing**.

## Single source of truth & references
- Primary API contracts come from the AWS SDK for Go v2 and official AWS docs.
- Local reference code lives in **/references/**. Treat it as READ-ONLY. Never copy large chunks verbatim.
- When using SDK types/clients, prefer exact imports from the **pinned** SDK version. Do not re-invent SDK types.

## Repository layout (unified & minimal)
- **/bin/**               # folder for binaries
- **/controller/**        # single controller: main.go, bedrock_client.go, reconcile.go, types.go (K8s types)
- **/crd/**               # CRD YAMLs (apiextensions.k8s.io/v1)
- **/cr/**                # example custom resources (YAML)
- **/tests/**             # unit tests (ignored by Git per request)
- **/references/**        # read-only reference repos & SDK snapshots (ignored by Git)
- **Makefile**            # build, test, docker targets
- **README.md**, **TASKS.md**, **.gitignore**, **go.mod**

> Note: We are **not** using Kubebuilder or Operator SDK. The controller will use client-go/controller patterns directly (workqueue, informers, rate-limited retries).

## Bootstrapping actions (execute once at project start)
- If repo is empty, generate these files:
  - **Makefile** (see “Makefile MUST provide”)
  - **.gitignore** with entries:
      /references/
      /tests/
      /bin/
      /dist/
      /vendor/
      .DS_Store
      .env
      .idea
      .vscode
      coverage.*
  - **go.mod** (module name asked interactively)
  - **README.md** (one-page overview + quickstart)
  - **TASKS.md** (task tracker; see “Tasking workflow & DoD”)
- Initialize Git and first commit:
  - Run: `git init -b main && git add . && git commit -m "chore: bootstrap unified bedrock controller"`
- Create first CRD & example **skeletons** (empty minimal fields) so tests can compile.

## Tasking workflow & definition of done (DoD)
- From any complex user prompt, **create/append** to **TASKS.md** a checklist that Cursor will maintain.
- Cursor may propose intermediate tasks, **but must ask before inserting or reordering**.
- Each task must include:
  - **Goal**, **Changed files**, **Tests to add/update**, **Exit criteria** (objective & verifiable).
- **DoD** for every task:
  - `go build` succeeds; linters pass; **unit tests exist & pass** for touched code;
  - CRD and example CR updated **in lockstep** with controller/types;
  - README/CHANGELOG snippet updated if public surface changes.

## Iterative plan (four artifacts move together)
For each iteration, update the following in lockstep:
1) **Controller code** (`/controller/*.go`)
2) **CRD YAML** (`/crd/*.yaml`)
3) **Example CR** (`/cr/*.yaml`)
4) **Makefile** (ensure targets run locally & for deploy)

Cursor: when asked to add a feature, propose the **smallest vertical slice** that exercises all four, then wait for approval.

## Quality gates & coding standards
- Lint: `golangci-lint` default rules + govet + ineffassign. Fix or justify suppressions.
- Formatting: `gofmt` / `goimports`.
- Errors: wrap with `%w`; define sentinel errors for retryable cases.
- Logging: structured (zap/logr or std lib structured). No `fmt.Println` in prod paths.
- Concurrency: use client-go workqueue patterns; reconcile handlers must be **idempotent**.
- Config: load AWS region/creds from env/IRSA; never log secrets.

## AWS SDK for Go v2 usage rules
- **Pin versions** in `go.mod` (no `latest`).
- No network calls in **unit tests**. Define thin interfaces that wrap SDK clients; generate or hand-roll mocks.
- Centralize client construction in `/controller/bedrock_client.go`.
- Use context timeouts & retry middlewares; backoff with jitter on throttling.

## Kubernetes controller best practices (no Kubebuilder/Operator SDK)
- Use **client-go** informers/listers, SharedIndexInformer, and a **rate-limited workqueue**.
- Reconcile handler: read Spec, observe external state, converge → update Status/Conditions.
- **Finalizers**: add only when creating external resources; remove on clean teardown.
- **Status vs Spec**: Spec = desired; Status = observed (conditions with reason/message).
- RBAC: manage YAMLs under /crd or /cr (as needed for deployment), keep least privilege.
- Emit K8s **Events** for user-visible transitions and errors.

## Testing strategy
- **Phase 1: Local unit tests (strictly offline)**
  - Frameworks: `testing`, `testify/require`, `gomock` or `moq`.
  - Test **pure logic** (diff/merge desired vs observed) and **reconcile** via fake informer cache & mocked AWS client.
  - Golden files for YAML transformations under `/tests/testdata/`.
- **Phase 2: Local cluster smoke tests (opt-in after unit tests pass)**
  - When requested by the user, Cursor may assist by running **kubectl** commands (apply CRD/CR, inspect resources, logs) and **AWS CLI** calls (dry-run or low-risk `describe*`) to troubleshoot.
  - These are **manual/integration** steps, not part of `make test`. Cursor must **ask first** and show commands it plans to run.

## Makefile MUST provide
_Local default target: macOS (darwin/arm64). Deploy target: Linux (linux/amd64)._

- **Utilities**
  - `make tidy`        → `go mod tidy`
  - `make lint`        → `golangci-lint run`
  - `make test`        → run unit tests with `-race -coverprofile=coverage.out`
  - `make clean`       → remove build artifacts (dist/, bin/, coverage*)

- **Builds**
  - `make build-local`   → `GOOS=darwin GOARCH=arm64 CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath -ldflags "-s -w -X main.version=$(shell git describe --tags --always --dirty)" -o dist/controller-local ./controller`
  - `make build-deploy`  → `GOOS=linux  GOARCH=amd64 CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -trimpath -ldflags "-s -w -X main.version=$(shell git describe --tags --always --dirty)" -o dist/controller ./controller`

- **Docker**
  - `make docker-local`  → `docker buildx build --platform darwin/arm64 -t <image>:local .`
  - `make docker-deploy` → `docker buildx build --platform linux/amd64  -t <image>:<tag> .`

- **Run**
  - `make run`           → depends on **build-local**; runs the local binary using current `KUBECONFIG` with a clear warning if cluster access is detected.

- **Manifests / Generate (no Kubebuilder)**
  - `make crd-validate`  → validate `/crd/*.yaml` (e.g., using kubeconform/yamllint if installed; otherwise a placeholder).
  - `make cr-sync`       → helper that ensures **/controller/types.go** and **/crd/*.yaml** stay in sync (Cursor-maintained task; see “CRD lockstep rules”).
  - Note: We intentionally do **not** auto-generate CRDs from Go markers.

## Cross-compilation & reproducible builds
- **Local default**: `darwin/arm64` (Mac).
- **Deploy target**: `linux/amd64`.
- Use `-trimpath` and `-ldflags "-s -w"`; embed version via `-X main.version`.
- CGO disabled by default for static-ish binaries; document and justify if enabling CGO.

## CRD lockstep rules (no codegen)
- **Source of truth**: CRD YAMLs under `/crd/*.yaml`.
- Mirror the Spec/Status shapes in **`/controller/types.go`** (plain Go structs with `json` tags; no kubebuilder markers).
- Any change to fields:
  1) Update **CRD YAML** (validation schema, defaults, subresources).
  2) Update **Go types** in `/controller/types.go`.
  3) Update **reconcile** logic and **example CR** under `/cr/`.
  4) Run `make crd-validate` and `make test`.
- Cursor must modify **all related files in the same PR/diff** and annotate changes in **TASKS.md**.
- Keep **status** subresource enabled and use standard **Conditions** (`type`, `status`, `reason`, `message`, `lastTransitionTime`).

## Reference priority
- Prefer reading exact files in:
  - `@references/aws-sdk-go-v2/*`
  - `@references/bedrock/*` (if present)
- If a symbol is unclear, open the exact referenced file **and cite it in the PR description**.

## Prompts & diff discipline
- For any change request, produce:
  - **Minimal diff** (only changed files),
  - **New/updated unit tests**,
  - If public API changed, update **CRD + example CR + README**.
- Prefer editing specific files or selections. Avoid multi-file “big bangs” unless the task says so.

## Non-functional requirements
- Idempotency in reconcile loop (safe on retries).
- Respect AWS quotas; exponential backoff with jitter on throttling.
- Observability: structured logs + minimal metrics (reconcile count/duration, result, retries).
- Security: no secrets in logs; least-privileged AWS policies.

## Asking policy (Cursor must ask first)
- Before moving to the next **MAJOR** step or inserting new tasks, ask:
  - “Proposed next tasks: … Proceed? [y/N]”
- If ambiguity exists (resource names, namespaces, AWS account/region), ask to confirm.

## Initial task list (seed into TASKS.md on first run)
- [ ] **Bootstrap repo** (Makefile, go.mod, .gitignore, README, TASKS.md; init Git; first commit)
- [ ] **Define initial CRD**: `BedrockAgent` (minimal Spec/Status) in `/crd/bedrockagent.yaml` (status subresource enabled)
- [ ] **Mirror types** in `/controller/types.go` to match CRD Spec/Status (json tags)
- [ ] **Example CR** in `/cr/bedrockagent-sample.yaml` matching the CRD
- [ ] **Controller skeleton** in `/controller/main.go` + `/controller/reconcile.go` + `/controller/bedrock_client.go` (client interface only; no real AWS calls)
- [ ] **Unit tests** for reconcile logic with **mocked AWS client** and fake informer cache
- [ ] **Makefile**: build-local, build-deploy, docker-local, docker-deploy, test, lint, run, crd-validate
- [ ] **Run tests locally** (`make test`) and fix failures
- [ ] **(Optional, ask first) Local cluster smoke**: apply CRD & sample CR via kubectl; inspect controller logs; optional AWS CLI `describe*` calls for read-only validation
- [ ] Plan next vertical slice (e.g., KnowledgeBase, Guardrails, InferenceProfiles), then repeat the 4-artifact loop

## Commit & PR hygiene
- Conventional commits (feat:, fix:, chore:, docs:, refactor:, test:, ci:).
- Each PR references tasks completed from **TASKS.md**; include rationale and links to referenced SDK files.
- No failing tests in PRs; if flaky, mark and create a follow-up task to deflake.

## Guardrails & constraints
- No network calls in **unit** tests.
- Don’t bypass lint rules without comment.
- Keep public API changes explicit; never silently mutate CRD schemas.
- Keep `/tests/` and `/references/` **out of Git**, as requested.

## What to do now (Cursor)
- If repo is empty, propose **module name** and **image name**, then:
  - Generate **Makefile**, **go.mod**, **.gitignore**, **README.md**, **TASKS.md**, minimal CRD + example CR, and controller skeleton.
  - Ask before adding extra tooling (golangci-lint config, kubeconform, etc.).
- After confirmation, execute the “Bootstrap repo” task and mark it done in **TASKS.md**, then propose the next two tasks.
